  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-24T02:50:58.162Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I would like an animation behavior to be added that allows me to disable VRChat's current behavior of having the avatar rotate to follow the user's head.\nThis behavior exists when using 3 or 4 point tracking, but not full body tracking. When using full body tracking, the avatar only rotates when the joystick is used.\nI'm developing an animation controller that would allow someone using 3 or 4 point tracking to use poses like those using full body tracking, and this issue prevents an ideal implementation.\nThe only option that partway achieves this goal currently is setting up an animation state to disable locomotion entirely, but this is an undesirable way to do it.",
